## $issueKey/$issueId come from PanelContextProvider (declared on the
## web-panel module) — NOT from $issue, which is not reliably present in the
## web-panel velocity context on Jira 10.3 (confirmed live: both attributes
## rendered blank). Quiet references ($!) render empty rather than literal
## text if a value is ever missing; the JS bundle additionally falls back to
## AJS.Meta('issue-key') when the attributes are blank.
##
## Resources are NOT required here via $webResourceManager (variable absent
## from template contexts — confirmed live for the admin servlet): the
## panel-resources web-resource declares <context>jira.view.issue</context>
## and Jira auto-loads the bundle on every issue view; the bundle defers
## mounting until DOM-ready, so load order does not matter.
<div id="testplanit-panel"
     data-issue-key="$!issueKey"
     data-issue-id="$!issueId"></div>
